    "THE SECOND third-party key for this paper, and the first carrying ALL FOUR",
    "SERIES side by side. Not UPSC: no official key exists for this sitting and",
    "none is expected.",
    "",
    "INDEPENDENT OF THE DREAMERS KEY, and that is MEASURED rather than assumed --",
    "the two agree on only 135/150 = 90.0%. Two copies of one sheet would agree at",
    "or near 100%, so each carries its own evidence. This is what makes a",
    "disagreement between them informative instead of an echo.",
    "",
    "EXTRACTED TWICE BY INDEPENDENT METHODS, with 0 disagreements on all 150 x 4",
    "cells: once spatially, assigning each letter to the nearest SET- header by x",
    "centre, and once by reading order. The spatial pass is the one that matters,",
    "because the sheet prints twelve columns (three blocks x four series) and",
    "reading the wrong column does not fail -- it yields 150 confident WRONG",
    "entries, which is the documented risk on any multi-set key.",
    "",
    "ALL FOUR SERIES CARRY THE IDENTICAL LETTER DISTRIBUTION (A 36 / B 42 / C 33 /",
    "D 39). That is exactly what must hold when the series permute question ORDER",
    "but not OPTIONS, and it corroborates the 0 PERMUTED result our own Set D",
    "fidelity match reached from the other direction.",
    "",
    "THE SET-D COLUMN VALIDATED OUR FIDELITY MAP FROM OUTSIDE OUR OWN TOOLING.",
    "Pushing this sheet Set-A column through data/2026-2-D.map.json reproduces",
    "this sheet own Set-D column 150/150, with a deliberately shifted control",
    "scoring 17.3%. Centurion derived that correspondence by reading the booklets;",
    "we derived ours by matching option text. They agree on every question.",
    "",
    "The disclaimer claims star marks on doubtful answers. THERE ARE NONE --",
    "checked on the RENDERED page as well as the text layer, because a star drawn",
    "as vector art is invisible to a text parse. The yellow bands that read as",
    "highlighting are the watermark; they run at constant height across all three",
    "blocks."
